{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:pet-ch1-riemannian-submersion","title":"def:pet-ch1-riemannian-submersion","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics.md","line":82,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics.tex#def:pet-ch1-riemannian-submersion","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:pet-ch1-riemannian-manifold]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics.tex","label":"def:pet-ch1-riemannian-submersion","line":125,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Riemannian submersion]\n  \\label{def:pet-ch1-riemannian-submersion}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0023,petersen:page-0024}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch1-riemannian-manifold}\n\n  A submersion $F:(M,g_M)\\to(N,g_N)$ is a \\emph{Riemannian submersion} if\n  \\[\n    DF_p:(\\ker DF_p)^\\perp\\longrightarrow T_{F(p)}N\n  \\]\n  is a linear isometry for every $p\\in M$. Equivalently,\n  $g_M(v,w)=g_N(DF_pv,DF_pw)$ for horizontal $v,w$, or the adjoint\n  $(DF_p)^*:T_{F(p)}N\\to T_pM$ preserves inner products.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Riemannian submersion] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d6368312d7269656d616e6e69616e2d7375626d657273696f6e\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0023, petersen:page-0024</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_RiemannianMetrics%23def%3Apet-ch1-riemannian-manifold\">↗ def:pet-ch1-riemannian-manifold</a> <p></p>A submersion <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$F:(M,g_M)\\to (N,g_N)$\">$F:(M,g_M)\\to (N,g_N)$</span> is a <em>Riemannian submersion</em> if <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  DF_p:(\\ker DF_p)^\\perp \\longrightarrow T_{F(p)}N  \\]\">\\[  DF_p:(\\ker DF_p)^\\perp \\longrightarrow T_{F(p)}N  \\]</span> is a linear isometry for every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span>. Equivalently, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g_M(v,w)=g_N(DF_pv,DF_pw)$\">$g_M(v,w)=g_N(DF_pv,DF_pw)$</span> for horizontal <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v,w$\">$v,w$</span>, or the adjoint <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(DF_p)^*:T_{F(p)}N\\to T_pM$\">$(DF_p)^*:T_{F(p)}N\\to T_pM$</span> preserves inner products. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#rem:pet-ch1-nonlinear-isometric-immersion","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#ex:pet-ch1-orthogonal-projection","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:pet-ch1-riemannian-manifold","title":"def:pet-ch1-riemannian-manifold","label":"def:pet-ch1-riemannian-manifold"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#ex:pet-ch1-orthogonal-projection","title":"ex:pet-ch1-orthogonal-projection","label":"ex:pet-ch1-orthogonal-projection"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#ex:pet-ch1-hopf-fibration","title":"ex:pet-ch1-hopf-fibration","label":"ex:pet-ch1-hopf-fibration"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#rem:pet-ch1-quotient-submersion","title":"rem:pet-ch1-quotient-submersion","label":"rem:pet-ch1-quotient-submersion"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#rem:pet-ch1-covering-metric","title":"rem:pet-ch1-covering-metric","label":"rem:pet-ch1-covering-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#ex:pet-ch1-hopf-general-submersion","title":"ex:pet-ch1-hopf-general-submersion","label":"ex:pet-ch1-hopf-general-submersion"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#rem:pet-ch1-ex-2","title":"rem:pet-ch1-ex-2","label":"rem:pet-ch1-ex-2"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#rem:pet-ch1-ex-15","title":"rem:pet-ch1-ex-15","label":"rem:pet-ch1-ex-15"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#rem:pet-ch1-ex-18","title":"rem:pet-ch1-ex-18","label":"rem:pet-ch1-ex-18"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:pet-ch1-riemannian-submersion","title":"def:pet-ch1-riemannian-submersion","tex":"\\begin{definition}[Riemannian submersion]\n  \\label{def:pet-ch1-riemannian-submersion}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0023,petersen:page-0024}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch1-riemannian-manifold}\n\n  A submersion $F:(M,g_M)\\to(N,g_N)$ is a \\emph{Riemannian submersion} if\n  \\[\n    DF_p:(\\ker DF_p)^\\perp\\longrightarrow T_{F(p)}N\n  \\]\n  is a linear isometry for every $p\\in M$. Equivalently,\n  $g_M(v,w)=g_N(DF_pv,DF_pw)$ for horizontal $v,w$, or the adjoint\n  $(DF_p)^*:T_{F(p)}N\\to T_pM$ preserves inner products.\n\\end{definition}","source":"tex/references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:pet-ch1-riemannian-manifold","title":"def:pet-ch1-riemannian-manifold","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}